---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Surfaces">
  <h1>Surfaces</h1>
  <p>
    Structure is printed, not floated: panels are 2px ink rules, the table is
    the ledger and two one-column lists are its relatives, dividers are rules
    with fixed meanings, disclosures are programme notes, and tabs are
    departments on a rule.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PANEL</h2>
    <p>
      A <code>.mk-card</code> is a panel — a 2px ink rule around an inset
      fill. <code>--sunken</code> drops to a quiet 1px tan hairline for
      asides; <code>--flush</code> removes the padding so framed art meets
      the rule edge to edge.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-card mk-card--sunken">
      <strong>From the wings</strong>
      <p style="margin: var(--mk-space-xxs) 0 0; color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);">
        The quiet panel — a hairline aside that does not compete with boxed
        content.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mk-card mk-card--flush" style="margin-top: var(--mk-space-md); max-width: 18rem;">
      <img
        src={(import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/') + 'art/scene-config-water.jpg').replace(/\/+/g, '/')}
        alt="Wilson watering the config while Ake watches with alarm"
        width="1376" height="768" loading="lazy"
        style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;"
      />
      <div style="padding: var(--mk-panel-pad);">
        <strong>The water is the config</strong>
        <p style="margin: 2px 0 0; color: var(--mk-color-text-muted); font-style: italic;">change the water, not the fish</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-card"&gt;
  &lt;div class="mk-card mk-card--sunken"&gt;A quiet aside&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="mk-card mk-card--flush"&gt;&lt;img …&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE VERDICT</h2>
    <p>
      A stamp is the verdict struck across the thing it judges: paper caps on
      an ink slab, a few degrees off square because a hand holds a rubber
      stamp and a hand is never square. One word, never a sentence. The
      parent places it — give the panel <code>position: relative</code> and
      pick the corner — because a verdict belongs to the thing it is struck
      on, not to itself. Add <code>.mk-stamp-in</code> and it arrives on
      three frames and holds.
    </p>
    <div class="verdict-row">
      <div class="mk-card mk-card--sunken" style="position: relative; max-width: 20rem;">
        <strong>Wilson &middot; Over the Fence</strong>
        <p style="margin: var(--mk-space-xxs) 0 0; color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);">
          Eight nights, one hat, no face.
        </p>
        <span class="mk-stamp" style="position: absolute; top: -10px; right: 14px;">Ready</span>
      </div>
      <div class="mk-thumb mk-thumb--square" style="width: 13rem;">
        <img
          src={(import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, '/') + 'art/scene-ledger-fire.jpg').replace(/\/+/g, '/')}
          alt="The ledger goes up in flames while the company looks on"
          width="1024" height="1024" loading="lazy"
          style="width: 100%; height: auto; display: block;"
        />
        <span class="mk-stamp mk-stamp--danger" style="position: absolute; bottom: 18px; left: 10px;">Cancelled</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-card" style="position: relative"&gt;
  …
  &lt;span class="mk-stamp mk-stamp-in"
        style="position: absolute; top: -10px; right: 14px"&gt;Ready&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;span class="mk-stamp mk-stamp--danger"&gt;Cancelled&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE LEDGER</h2>
    <p>
      Typewriter caps over a 2px ink rule, Goudy figures on hairline rows,
      and a 3px double rule closing the account in <code>tfoot</code>.
      Numeric cells take <code>__num</code>; wrap the whole book in
      <code>.mk-table-wrap</code> so it scrolls inside its own rules.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-table-wrap">
      <table class="mk-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Act</th>
            <th scope="col" class="mk-table__num">Nights</th>
            <th scope="col" class="mk-table__num">Receipts</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Tim Taylor · More Power</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">12</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$1,240.50</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Wilson · Over the Fence</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">8</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$612.00</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Al Borland &amp; His Flannel Revue</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">5</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$301.25</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot>
          <tr>
            <td>IN TOTAL</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">25</td>
            <td class="mk-table__num">$2,153.75</td>
          </tr>
        </tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-table-wrap"&gt;
  &lt;table class="mk-table"&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col"&gt;Act&lt;/th&gt;
      &lt;th scope="col" class="mk-table__num"&gt;Receipts&lt;/th&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;Tim Taylor · More Power&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="mk-table__num"&gt;$1,240.50&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tbody&gt;
    &lt;tfoot&gt;&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;IN TOTAL&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="mk-table__num"&gt;$2,153.75&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/tfoot&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE DATELINE FEED</h2>
    <p>
      The ledger&rsquo;s one-column relative. The hour is stamped left in the
      column-head voice, the event is set right in prose, and a hairline
      divides the rows. Use it for joined, left, and status changed. The
      slug column is fixed, so every hour lines up; at phone width it takes
      its own line. No dots and no spine — the hairline is the division.
      Carry <code>role="list"</code>: a list with no marker loses its list
      role in WebKit, and the count and the position are what a screen
      reader needs from a feed.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The element contract is a list of <code>&lt;li&gt;</code>.</strong>
      <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code> is shown here because a feed has a real
      chronology; <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> takes the same class and renders
      identically. A <code>&lt;dl&gt;</code> does <em>not</em> &mdash; the
      row rules select <code>&gt; li</code>, so a definition list gets no
      grid, no hairline and no slug column. A time and its event look like a
      term and its definition, so this is worth saying out loud: convert the
      markup, do not reach for the class.
    </p>
    <ol class="mk-feed" role="list">
      <li>
        <span class="mk-feed__time">8:02 PM</span>
        <p class="mk-feed__event">Mr. Taylor joined the company.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mk-feed__time">8:14 PM</span>
        <p class="mk-feed__event">Mr. Borland took the flannel wardrobe off the bill.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mk-feed__time">8:31 PM</span>
        <p class="mk-feed__event">Mr. Wilson left, over the fence, as is his custom.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mk-feed__time">9:00 PM</span>
        <p class="mk-feed__event">The house went to SOLD OUT.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <pre><code>&lt;ol class="mk-feed" role="list"&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-feed__time"&gt;8:02 PM&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;p class="mk-feed__event"&gt;Mr. Taylor joined the company.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE WALK-THROUGH</h2>
    <p>
      A numbered instruction list for the steps the browser&rsquo;s own UI
      will not let you draw. It is a real <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>, so the
      order is semantics; the counter only prints it in the bill voice,
      &ldquo;No. 1 ·&rdquo;. The number comes from a CSS counter, so
      <code>start</code> and <code>value</code> do not move it — a
      walk-through starts at No. 1. Where a step points at a box the app
      cannot draw, stand in a <code>.mk-empty</code> dashed tile (see
      FEEDBACK).
    </p>
    <ol class="mk-steps">
      <li>
        <span class="mk-steps__act">Tap Share</span>
        <p class="mk-steps__note">
          The button at the foot of the browser — the one the management
          cannot draw for you.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mk-steps__act">Choose Add to Home Screen</span>
        <p class="mk-steps__note">Scroll the sheet; it sits below the printing options.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="mk-steps__act">Confirm</span>
        <p class="mk-steps__note">The bill takes its place among your other acts.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <pre><code>&lt;ol class="mk-steps"&gt;
  &lt;li&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-steps__act"&gt;Tap Share&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;p class="mk-steps__note"&gt;The button at the foot of the browser.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PRINTED RULES</h2>
    <p>
      Rules do the dividing, and each weight has a fixed meaning. Pick the
      rule for what the break means, not for taste. The accent rule spends
      the ochre ration — use it once, if at all.
    </p>
    <p class="rule-note">default · 1px tan — a minor division</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider" />
    <p class="rule-note">--thick · 2px ink — a department underline</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--thick" />
    <p class="rule-note">--double · 4px double — a major section break</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double" />
    <p class="rule-note">--double-thin · 3px double — the footer break</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double-thin" />
    <p class="rule-note">--dash · nothing is printed here yet</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--dash" />
    <p class="rule-note">--accent · the ochre rule — rationed</p>
    <hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--accent" />
    <p class="rule-note">--label · a typewriter slug flanked by hairlines</p>
    <div class="mk-divider mk-divider--label"><span>intermission</span></div>
    <pre><code>&lt;hr class="mk-divider" /&gt;
&lt;hr class="mk-divider mk-divider--double" /&gt;
&lt;div class="mk-divider mk-divider--label"&gt;&lt;span&gt;intermission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PROGRAMME NOTES</h2>
    <p>
      Native <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> between hairline rules. The marker
      is a typewriter + that becomes &minus; when the note is open — the
      glyph swaps instantly, like set type.
    </p>
    <details class="mk-disclosure">
      <summary>A NOTE ON THE PYROTECHNICS</summary>
      <div class="mk-disclosure__body">
        The management wishes to assure patrons that the flames in Act II are
        entirely intentional, and that Mr. Borland stands in the wings with
        the extinguisher as always.
      </div>
    </details>
    <details class="mk-disclosure" open>
      <summary>ON THE MATTER OF THE FENCE</summary>
      <div class="mk-disclosure__body">
        Mr. Wilson appears by arrangement with his garden, and is seen only
        to the brim of his hat. Add the <code>open</code> attribute to unfold
        a note on load.
      </div>
    </details>
    <pre><code>&lt;details class="mk-disclosure"&gt;
  &lt;summary&gt;A NOTE ON THE PYROTECHNICS&lt;/summary&gt;
  &lt;div class="mk-disclosure__body"&gt;…&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/details&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>DEPARTMENTS</h2>
    <p>
      Tabs are departments on a 2px ink rule; the current department
      overprints it with its own ink underline. Selection answers to
      <code>aria-selected</code>, <code>aria-current</code>, or
      <code>--active</code> — the styling hook is the semantics. Tabs wrap
      rather than overflow the rule.
    </p>
    <div class="mk-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Departments of the house">
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true">Stage</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Carpentry</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Wardrobe</button>
      <button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false">Front of house</button>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;div class="mk-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Departments"&gt;
  &lt;button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true"&gt;Stage&lt;/button&gt;
  &lt;button class="mk-tabs__tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false"&gt;Carpentry&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE PAGER</h2>
    <p>
      The neighbouring acts, named. &ldquo;&larr; THE PREVIOUS &middot; No. 1
      of 3 &middot; THE NEXT &rarr;&rdquo; does not fit a 358px column, and
      numbering the acts is wrong anyway &mdash; nobody thinks of their
      Thursday group as No. 2. The arrows carry the neighbour&rsquo;s name,
      which is the only thing a reader wants to know before moving.
      <strong>No count, no numbering.</strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      The dots are printed <strong>squares</strong>, the current one inked
      solid &mdash; square like the badge&rsquo;s status dot, because the
      medallion is the only round thing in the system. They carry position
      and nothing else, so the row is <code>aria-hidden</code> and the
      neighbour names in the <code>aria-label</code>s carry the meaning. The
      <code>__label</code> span is required: it is what clips a long act name
      instead of widening the column.
    </p>
    <div class="pager-demo">
      <nav class="mk-pager" aria-label="Squads">
        <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__prev" href="#" aria-label="Previous: Raid Night">
          <span class="mk-pager__label">Raid Night</span>
        </a>
        <span class="mk-pager__dots" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="mk-pager__dot"></span>
          <span class="mk-pager__dot mk-pager__dot--current"></span>
          <span class="mk-pager__dot"></span>
        </span>
        <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__next" href="#" aria-label="Next: Tabletop">
          <span class="mk-pager__label">Tabletop</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <p class="rule-note">two acts only &middot; the dots row is optional</p>
    <div class="pager-demo">
      <nav class="mk-pager" aria-label="Acts">
        <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__prev" href="#" aria-label="Previous: The Amazing Flannel Brothers">
          <span class="mk-pager__label">The Amazing Flannel Brothers</span>
        </a>
        <a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__next" href="#" aria-label="Next: Wardrobe">
          <span class="mk-pager__label">Wardrobe</span>
        </a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <pre><code>&lt;nav class="mk-pager" aria-label="Squads"&gt;
  &lt;a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__prev" href="/raid-night"
     aria-label="Previous: Raid Night"&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-pager__label"&gt;Raid Night&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;span class="mk-pager__dots" aria-hidden="true"&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-pager__dot"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-pager__dot mk-pager__dot--current"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-pager__dot"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;a class="mk-btn mk-btn--ghost mk-pager__next" href="/tabletop"
     aria-label="Next: Tabletop"&gt;
    &lt;span class="mk-pager__label"&gt;Tabletop&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* The phone column, so the clipping constraint is visible. */
    .pager-demo {
      max-width: 24rem;
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
    }

    .rule-note {
      margin: var(--mk-space-md) 0 0;
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);
    }

    .verdict-row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: var(--mk-space-lg);
      align-items: flex-start;
    }

    /* Tighten the demo rules so the meanings read as a chart. */
    .rule-note + .mk-divider {
      margin: var(--mk-space-xs) 0 0;
    }

    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
